# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel environment — paste these into Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The build does NOT need any of them. Verified: `next build` completes with every
# service unreachable, because every data loader degrades to an empty result rather
# than throwing, and no page prerenders against the database. Vercel will go green
# on the first deploy; the storefront will render its own design with empty shelves
# until DATABASE_URL points somewhere real.
#
# Fill them in the order below — each one lights up more of the store.

# ── 1. Required now: the session cookie is signed with this ──────────────────
# GENERATE YOUR OWN. This file is tracked in a public repository, so a value written here is a
# value anybody can read — and anybody who can read the signing key can mint a session cookie for
# any account. lib/session.ts refuses to start signing without one rather than falling back.
#
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
#
# then paste the output into the Vercel project's environment variables, not into this file.
SESSION_SECRET=

# ── 2. Media — already works, nothing to set ─────────────────────────────────
# storage/media is committed to the repo (207 MB: product photographs, the 37
# category images, the estimator's house renders) and served by app/media/[...key].
# Move to S3/CloudFront later by setting MEDIA_STORE=s3 + S3_BUCKET + S3_REGION.
MEDIA_STORE=local
MEDIA_ROOT=./storage/media
MEDIA_BASE_URL=/media
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_NAME=Build Objects

# ── 3. The catalogue: this is what turns empty shelves into a store ──────────
# Any MySQL 8 host — PlanetScale, Aiven, Railway, RDS. Restore the shipped dump:
#     mysql -h <host> -u <user> -p <db> < infra/seed/buildobjects.sql
# 16 tables, 27 SKUs, 509 specifications. Personal tables ship empty by design.
DATABASE_URL=mysql://user:password@host:3306/buildobjects

# ── 4. Search — /search and the header suggestions ──────────────────────────
# Without it those two surfaces are empty; every other page works.
MEILI_HOST=https://your-instance.meilisearch.io
MEILI_MASTER_KEY=

# ── 5. Queue — only the pipeline uses it. The storefront does not. ──────────
# Leave unset on Vercel: QUEUE_DRIVER=auto falls back to the MySQL-backed driver.
QUEUE_DRIVER=auto
# REDIS_URL=

# ── 6. Optional: the AI features degrade honestly without these ─────────────
# AR scene understanding runs ON DEVICE now (packages/ar-engine/src/vision) and
# needs no key at all. Gemini only refines it when present.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
